WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.220
We'd like to thank Audible for supporting
PBS.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.060
It can happen a million ways.

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:10.090
Maybe you lost your job and had to choose
a utility charge to ignore.

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:13.420
Or maybe you’ve developed a serious health
condition and now you’re stuck with a whopping

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:14.420
medical bill.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.780
Or maybe...you just forgot to change your
address and a bill went to the wrong place!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.380
At some point in your life, you might find
yourself having descended to another world

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.580
known as debt collections.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.330
And you wouldn’t be alone down there.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:33.280
In 2019, the CFPB reported that more than
1 in 4 Americans have a debt that’s currently

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.000
in third party collections.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.820
But there are actually different levels to
this world with different opponents and obstacles

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.820
to face.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.370
They each require a different set of strategies
to make it through with your dignity and finances

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.370
intact.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:52.220
So today we’re going to be your personal
guides to the 4 levels of debt collection.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.940
This whole situation probably began when you
passed the 30 days late mark on paying a debt

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.050
or a bill.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:11.750
At which point they probably sent you a notification
which you may have ignored or missed.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.350
Welcome, you’ve now entered the first level
of the debt collections process.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:21.280
Technically, your lender can report this late
payment to the credit bureau right after you

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.409
pass the 30 day mark, but many will continue
to give you grace for an extra 30 days.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:31.010
This is a critical juncture where you have
the power to stop your descent.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:35.130
Believe it or not, your lender WANTS to have
a good relationship with you.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:39.640
Fighting you by putting your debt further
down the levels of collections is costly,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.270
so being proactive and up front with them
is the best way to go.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.159
Ideally, the moment it becomes clear you can’t
pay a bill when it’s due, call them, explain

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:49.439
the situation.

00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:53.750
You might be able to get on a plan and prevent
yourself from sinking lower.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.380
Once you pass the 60 day mark, things start
to heat up.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.040
You might get one of those notifications on
your phone from a credit-tracking service

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.790
telling you your credit score dropped by as
much as 100 points!

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.060
That’s also when you’ll start getting
calls and more letters trying to collect the

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.060
payment.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.329
Let’s think of this as level 1.5 because
during this time, you’re most likely dealing

00:02:14.329 --> 00:02:18.299
with the original creditor and while your
credit may have taken a hit there’s still

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:21.810
a very high chance you can negotiate directly
with them.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:27.370
Once you get to the point where the debt is
90 to 180 days late, you have crossed the

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.719
River Styx and are solidly in the second ring
of collections hell.

00:02:31.719 --> 00:02:36.340
The original lender has written you off as
a lost cause and “charged off” your account.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.519
If it hasn’t already, your credit score
is going to tank and you’ll probably start

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:43.739
getting some aggressive phone calls from new
people.

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:47.599
This is because many lenders will bring in
a third-party “Collections Agency” acting

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:48.750
as a middle man.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.639
Their aim is to get you to pay as much as
possible as fast as possible.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:58.200
It’s not uncommon for the person on the
phone to earn a commission between 25% - 45%

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.650
of the amount you pay, hence the urgency you
might sense in their voice.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.680
But remember, it’s not too late to negotiate
your balance down!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:12.180
Experts say it’s not uncommon to end up
settling for 30 - 70% of the original balance.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.379
So start your negotiations with a small amount,
and see how flexible they are.

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:21.120
Also, here’s a pro-tip, call them at the
end of the month.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.340
Most collectors work on monthly quotas.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:29.290
And they may be more amenable to a deeper
discount as the end of the month approaches.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:34.360
But don’t make them any offers until you
have received a “debt validation letter”.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.370
Collectors are required to send these within
5 days of initially contacting you, and it

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.319
will detail what the debt is and how much
you owe.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:45.260
Make sure to check this against your records
-- you don’t want to pay a debt that isn’t

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.639
yours or to a company that can’t prove they
actually own it.

00:03:48.639 --> 00:03:51.980
You also don’t have to go through this process
alone.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:57.139
Once you’re past that first level of collections,
reaching out to a non-profit debt-counselor

00:03:57.139 --> 00:04:02.540
can be an incredibly helpful move, especially
if you have lates with multiple lenders.

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.879
These situations can get very tricky and the
rules can change depending on your specific

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:08.879
situation.

00:04:08.879 --> 00:04:10.760
It might not even cost you anything.

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:15.269
All agencies certified by the National Foundation
for Credit Counseling will offer free credit

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:16.950
counseling sessions.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.480
After the 180 day mark, the bank, medical
provider, or credit card company may give

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.960
up trying to collect through the collections
agency.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.960
Phew!

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.640
You’re off the hook now, right?

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.640
Probably not.

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:32.420
Instead of writing off your debt as a total
loss, they will often SELL your debt to a

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.330
“Debt Buyer”, hoping to make a little
of their money back.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:42.790
This means you’ve arrived at the third and
often final level: the realm of debt-buyers.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.890
These companies will bid to buy bundles of
“bad-debts” at a steep discount.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:53.220
For example, if you had a $1,000 debt that
was sold to a debt-buyer, odds are they only

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.320
paid $20 or $30 for it.

00:04:55.320 --> 00:05:01.290
Debt-buyers only expect to collect 3-6% of
the balances they own, so keep that in mind

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.530
as you negotiate.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.540
Again, low-ball first and see where it gets
you.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:11.430
And be sure to not give them personal information
up front; let them tell you what they have

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.430
on you.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:16.250
This can protect you against shady collectors
and con artists.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:22.150
You also need to be careful about reviving
an old debt that’s past the statute of limitations!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:26.820
Collectors have a limited window of time in
which to sue you for debts, depending on the state.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.640
Here in Texas, it’s only 4 years--from the
date of your last payment!

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:34.870
So if a collector can convince you to make
a payment on a debt that’s 3 years and 11

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.970
months old, the clock resets!

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.980
So I know what you must be thinking...wow!

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.430
I can just wait it out a few years and my
debt will go away!

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:47.980
And yes, some old debts will fall off your
credit report after 7 years.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:53.370
But, remember, your credit score and history
are constantly being checked by utilities,

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.950
rentals companies and even employers.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:01.430
So unless you plan on not making a single
move in living or employment situation for

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:04.870
7 whole years, you should attempt to deal
with it.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:09.270
Debt buyers can often be the toughest and
most aggressive in their communication.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:13.650
Be sure to review the Fair Debt Collection
Practices Act so you know what they are and

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:15.470
aren’t allowed to do.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:19.500
Calling you late at night, contacting family
members, or threatening you with arrest are

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.470
all strictly forbidden.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.310
Debtors prison is not a thing anymore.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.860
You cannot be thrown in jail for a debt.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.700
And if you ask them to stop calling you at
work, they are supposed to respect that request.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.390
If a collector is violating these rules, you
are entitled to submit a complaint to the

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:37.520
CFPB website and your state’s attorney general’s
office.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:42.160
Sometimes though, instead of ending up with
a debt buyer, the original creditor can choose

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.470
to take you to court.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:47.940
Since they’ll have to pay an attorney, they’re
unlikely to do this over small balances.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:54.810
But if you ever do find yourself on the receiving
end of a summons, do not ignore it.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:59.410
Not showing up to court means that the other
side wins automatically and will have the

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:03.060
right to do things like garnish your wages
or seize assets.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:08.750
At this point, it’s best to seek professional
legal advice.There are organizations that

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.760
will provide legal aid to debtors for little
to no cost.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:15.980
Again, speaking with a local debt counselor
is a good place to start.

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:20.980
As you can see, the landscape of collections
changes depending on the level you find yourself in.

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:23.360
So it’s important to adjust your tactics
accordingly.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:29.360
And remember, the lower you go, the more likely
collectors will benefit from preying on feelings

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.080
of shame and confusion.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.510
Don’t give them the upper hand by losing
your temper, playing loose with facts or being

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.280
afraid to ask for help.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.860
That way you can beat the heat and claw your
way back to the surface.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.700
And that’s our Two Cents!

